# Control structures

## Flags

**True** = `-1` (all bits set); **false** = `0`. Comparisons produce canonical flags. In `if`, any non-zero value is treated as true — still prefer `-1`/`0`.

```forth
: positive? ( n -- flag )
  0> ;

: min-no-if ( n1 n2 -- n )
  2dup < if nip else drop then ;
```

Use `0=` / `0<>` to canonicalize. Combine flags with `and` / `or` / `xor` to avoid `if` when both branches are simple (e.g., `0= 14 and`).

Do not assume `1` is true.

## if / else / then

```forth
: abs ( n -- |n| )
  dup 0< if negate then ;
```

Each branch must leave the **same** stack effect unless documented otherwise.

## begin / until / again / while / repeat

```forth
: wait-key ( -- key )
  begin key? until key ;
```

`2/` floors toward zero; `/` rounds toward zero — pick the one your algorithm needs.

## counted loops

```forth
: fill ( c addr u -- )
  0 ?do dup i + c! loop drop ;
```

Index: `i` (inner), `j` (nested). Bounds: `( limit start -- )` for `?do` / `+loop`.

## Early exit

```forth
: find-it ( u -- flag )
  0 ?do  i  target = if  i unloop exit  then  loop  false ;
```

- `leave` — exit innermost counted loop (calls `unloop` internally).
- `exit` — exit current colon definition; each enclosing loop needs `unloop` before `exit`.

## Recursion

```forth
: fac ( n -- n! )
  dup 0> if  dup 1- recurse *  else  drop 1  then ;
```

Use `recursive` (Gforth) or `recurse` to call the word under definition. Redefining a core word (e.g., `/`) shadows the old version inside the new body only.

## return stack in loops

`>r` / `r>` / `r@` for temporary storage — document `(R …)` and balance on every exit path.

**Do not mix `>r`/`r@` with `DO` / `?DO`.** Loop counter and limit live on the return stack; `R@` inside the loop returns `I`, not your saved value. Alternatives:

- keep the value on the data stack (`over` / `rot`);
- use a `VALUE` or Gforth `{ locals }` (see `forth-dialect-gforth.mdc`);
- use `BEGIN … WHILE … REPEAT` instead of `DO`.

`2swap` via return stack: `rot >r rot r>` — see `forth-anti-patterns.mdc` for leak traps.

## case / of / endof (if available)

Dispatch on discrete values; keep each `of` branch stack-balanced.

## State smart words

Words like `if` are immediate — see `forth-meta.mdc`. Do not manually `compile,` control words unless building defining words.
